data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-summary.md\", \"content\": \"# d002 — greet, tested\\n\\n## What I implemented\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a `greet(name)` function that returns `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`\\n   with `name` substituted in.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — unittest `TestCase` with two tests:\\n   - `test_normal_name`: `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - `test_empty_string`: `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n   (The test file inserts `src/` onto `sys.path` so it can `import greet`\\n   without needing a package/`__init__.py` setup.)\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nRan from the repository root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n```\\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit code: `0`.\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nCommitted to my own branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>` as a\\nnormal new commit (no history rewritten):\\n\\n- `ddc9896` — \\\"Add greet function with unit tests\\\" (2 files changed,\\n  21 insertions), on top of base `1053761f6a654e7ea58deb67a671a00d2e7fc8ac`.\\n\\n## Notes / caveats\\n\\n- Nothing was skipped or blocked; the dispatch was implemented exactly as\\n  specified.\\n- `__pycache__` directories were created by running the tests but were not\\n  added to git (left untracked, no `.gitignore` existed to update and none\\n  was requested).\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

